---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'September 2, 2026';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy - Maddie Tavares">
	<PageHeader
		title="Privacy Policy"
		lede={`Last updated ${lastUpdated}`}
	/>

	<article class="policy">
		<p>
			This site (maddietavares.dev) is a personal portfolio.
			It doesn't sell anything or run ads, and it collects very little information about
			visitors. This page explains what is collected, why, and by whom.
		</p>

		<h2>Hosting &amp; server logs</h2>
		<p>
			This site is hosted on <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vercel</a>.
			Like most hosts, Vercel automatically logs standard request data for every visit —
			things like IP address, browser/device type, referring page, and request timestamps —
			for security, performance, and abuse-prevention purposes. I don't have a dashboard of
			this data myself; it's handled under Vercel's own privacy policy, linked above.
		</p>

		<h2>Cookies &amp; tracking</h2>
		<p>
			This site does not use analytics, advertising, or tracking cookies. No cookie banner is
			shown because no non-essential cookies are set.
		</p>

		<h2>Contact form</h2>
		<p>
			The <a href="/contact">Contact</a> page includes a form for reaching out. When you submit
			it, your name, email address, and message are sent
			to <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Formspree</a>,
			a third-party form service, which forwards the submission to my personal email inbox.
			I use that information only to reply to you — it isn't added to any mailing list, sold,
			or shared with anyone else. Formspree's own privacy policy governs how they handle the
			data in transit and in their systems.
		</p>

		<h2>Third-party links</h2>
		<p>
			This site links out to places like GitHub and LinkedIn. Those sites have their own
			privacy policies, which I'd encourage you to check if you're curious how they handle
			your data.
		</p>

		<h2>Children's privacy</h2>
		<p>
			This site isn't directed at children, and I don't knowingly collect information from
			anyone under 13.
		</p>

		<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
		<p>
			If what this site collects ever changes (for example, if analytics are added later),
			this page will be updated and the date above will reflect the change.
		</p>

		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>
			Questions about this policy? Reach out via the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
		</p>
	</article>
</Layout>

<style>
	.policy {
		width: var(--page-content-width);
		margin: 0 0 0 auto;
	}

	.policy h2 {
		font-family: var(--font-heading);
		font-size: 1.3rem;
		margin: var(--space-4) auto var(--space-1) auto;
		max-width: 42rem;
	}

	.policy p {
		line-height: 1.6;
		margin: 0 auto;
		max-width: 42rem;
	}

	.policy a {
		color: var(--color-primary-dark);
	}

	@media (max-width: 860px) {
		.policy {
			width: 100%;
			margin: 0 auto;
		}
	}
</style>
